AI Features

AI CV Reader

The user uploads an existing CV as a Word document or PDF. The CVReader class reads the document, sends the text to OpenAI GPT-4o-mini with a structured prompt, and receives back a JSON object containing all extracted details. These are then used to auto fill the entire form.

AI Profile Summary Generator

Once the user has filled in their details, they can click Generate Summary with AI. Flask collects the form data, builds a personalised prompt including the user's name, skills, education, experience and the target country's tone, and sends it to OpenAI. The summary is returned and automatically filled into the summary field. The user can click again to get a completely different version.


Project Structure

app.py                   # Main Flask application and all routes
models/
    country.py           # Country class — stores CV rules per country
    user.py              # User class — stores personal details from form
    cv.py                # CV class — combines User and Country
    pdf_generator.py     # PDFGenerator class — builds the PDF using ReportLab
    cv_reader.py         # CVReader class — AI powered CV reading using OpenAI
templates/
    home.html            # Landing page
    index.html           # Country selection page
    cv_form.html         # CV form with AI features
static/css/
    style.css            # Main stylesheet including dark mode
data/
    countries.json       # Country data
output/                  # Generated PDFs (not tracked in git)


OOP Class Structure

The project uses five classes each with a single responsibility:


Country — stores the CV formatting rules for each supported country
User — stores the personal and professional details entered by the user
CV — combines a User object and a Country object into a formatted CV
PDFGenerator — takes a CV object and generates a two column PDF file
CVReader — reads an uploaded CV file and uses OpenAI to extract key details



Getting Started

Prerequisites


Python 3.10 or higher
pip
An OpenAI API key


Installation


Clone the repository:


bashgit clone https://github.com/Vyshna-Work/CVCompass.git
cd CVCompass


Install dependencies:


bashpip install flask reportlab python-docx PyMuPDF openai python-dotenv


Create a .env file in the root folder and add your OpenAI API key:


OPENAI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here


Run the app:


bashpython app.py


Visit http://localhost:5000 in your browser.



Deployment

CVCompass is deployed on PythonAnywhere and accessible at:
cvcompass.pythonanywhere.com

No installation required — works in any browser for free.


